  "description": "What: a ROUTINE civilian car at the checkpoint (CE-4622 K-4/K-6, docs/designs/vehicle-tactics/DESIGN_Checkpoint_And_Ramming.md CP-1, CP-2, CP-4) on basic-desert: the squad 'Checkpoint' (Stopper, Searcher 1, Searcher 2, Rifleman, Gunner with an M249) runs Checkpoint on the 'Checkpoint approach' route (stop line x 380). A Neutral 'Car' with its 'Driver' drives east from x 100 at 12 m/s and slows (5 m/s at x 330) to stop at the line. Judge: (1) the checkpoint signals it (the Stopper's Warning gesture) and never fires (2) it reads ROUTINE (3) the Driver gets out with his hands up, he and the car are searched and RELEASED (he boards again). Fail: any shot at the car; a threat; no search."
 },
